Corridor supports one released database head and its immediate successor.

`b7d3f9a1c2e5` builds the consolidated August 2026 schema. `c0a1d0b5e11e`
canonicalizes equivalent check expressions. `0ca809014df7` adds immutable
spreadsheet Source Segments. `444758f7b4a7` adds typed Facts, `d430a1b2c3d4`
makes released Reports reference artifact-owned content, and `1142da5be661`
adds the scoped append receipt. `1d2e3f4a5b6c` adds PDF page inventory/failure
history. `961bd259310f` adds immutable Extracted Proposals and is the current
released predecessor. `437e8c9a0b1d` adds Minutes prose spans and pending
statement wording Facts. `20c7d970be63` adds typed inclusion decisions and is
the current released head. `452c7d8e9f10` is its one supported successor: it
adds durable prose completeness accounting. Fresh and upgraded databases have
one exact schema fingerprint.

Executable revisions live in `baseline_versions`. `versions` is not configured
as an Alembic version location; it retains only inert bytes required by released
policy fingerprints.

Add one linear successor for a schema change. Test a fresh baseline and the
released-head-to-successor path with representative rows. Retire that transition
test after all supported databases advance and the released head moves forward.
Downgrade across a consolidated baseline is unsupported.
